Eighth Edition source and data, imported because v10src carries none.

Admin/etcfiles names seventeen files that no v10 tape has.  Six are per-machine
data and four cannot be recovered at all (analyze and catman are 4.3BSD's --
etc/catman.c and old/analyze.c -- while backsh and dklisten appear nowhere in
any BSD, in v10's own manual, or anywhere in the corpus but etcfiles itself).
The rest are here, byte-identical to the v8 tree in this repository:

    finddev.c  fstat.c  rp07dump.c  rp07rest.c   from v8/usr/src/cmd
    install.sh                                   from v8/usr/src/cmd

They live under build/ rather than in v10/usr/src so that nothing in the
distribution tree pretends to be tape content.  ./patch copies them into
$SRC/cmd before the build (patch:122), the way it does the two gcc
reconstructions.

Data no v10 tape carries, which v10 programs read by name, came the same way
on 8 Oct 2026 -- again byte-identical to this repository's v8/:

    words      from v8/usr/dict/words        look(1), hangman
    lib.b      from v8/usr/lib/lib.b         bc -l
    fortunes   from v8/usr/games/lib         fortune
    quiz.k/    from v8/usr/games/lib/quiz.k  quiz, all 34 files
    cunumber   from v8/usr/lib/cunumber      cu; empty in v8 too

These are installed by the mkfile, not copied by patch: they are products,
not sources.  The mkfile comment above their rules records what each was
checked against in the program that reads it.

../etc holds the same for files that are shipped rather than compiled:

    mklost+found  shutdown  group     from v8/etc
    whoami                            ours: the machine name, ipnx-v10
    dst                               ours: the US daylight-saving rules
                                      since 1967, for ctime's /lib/dst
    Units  Monetary.Units             generated by tools/v10-units.py from
                                      cmd/units/old/usr.lib.units
    hyphen.tex                        Knuth's, unmodified, from Plan 9's
                                      sys/lib/texmf/tex/generic/hyphen --
                                      TeX's patterns, for troff's ALTHYPHENS
    mtab  utmp                        empty, as they are in v8 -- runtime
                                      state that mount and login write
